   [campaign]    [soul] ORACLE decision: kind=action ctx={'place': 'You\'re in the Cerulean Gym — indoors, inside a building (rooms and doors — NOT a cave).. Places you\'ve been with wild Pokémon you can walk back to: Route 4; Route 24; an unfamiliar area. You can walk to anywhere you\'ve already been.. Okay — to get past this I need HM Surf — the prize of the Safari Zone\'s Secret House, deep in the back area. Surf opens the sea: Cinnabar, the Seafoam route, and Victory Road\'s water.. HOW POKÉMON WORKS (what you\'re playing for): the GOAL is to earn 8 Gym Badges, beat the Elite Four, and roll the credits — that\'s beating the game. You build a TEAM of up to 6 Pokémon you like AND that cover each other (types/roles) — a solo carry with a dead-weight bench is a losing setup; a real trainer fields a balanced, levelled squad. CATCHING wild Pokémon is central (\'gotta catch \'em all\') — you catch to build that team and to fill the Pokédex. When you meet a wild Pokémon, weigh it: is it cool/strong/useful, does it cover a gap, is it better than a bench-warmer? — keep your best ~6, and build a squad you actually like. THE ARC: build a team -> beat the 8 gyms prepared -> Elite Four -> credits. ALSO NORMAL: you entered your own name (and your rival\'s) when the game began — people in this world knowing your names is ordinary, not a mystery to react to. RIGHT NOW your team is thin/lopsided (a strong lead but weak or too few others) — that\'s why tough trainers wall you. Building up a real squad (catch a good new teammate, level the weak ones) is how a prepared trainer gets past these. THE MAIN QUEST IS A FIXED PATH you\'re always on: beat the 8 Gym Leaders in order, then the Elite Four, then you win the game. You\'re on GYM 2 of 8 — next is Misty in Cerulean City. The road forward leads there: until you\'ve won you are ALWAYS making progress toward the next gym. Grinding/catching/detours are fine — but ONLY with a clear purpose, and then you GET BACK ON THE ROAD to Cerulean City. Never just circle the same grass. ⚠️ ORDER OF OPERATIONS: before Misty, HM Surf — the prize of the Safari Zone\'s Secret House, deep in the back area. Surf opens the sea: Cinnabar, the Seafoam route, and Victory Road\'s water — that errand comes FIRST (it unblocks the road and the trainers along it are exactly the training you need). Misty is step two, not a competing choice. Word on the road about Misty: she runs WATER-types — a whole gym over a pool; grass and electric do the work YOUR STORY SO FAR (what you\'ve actually done — your past, not the future): You started in Pallet Town, crossed Route 1-2 and Viridian Forest, and beat Brock in Pewter City for the Boulder Badge. Now you\'re pushing on toward the next gym.. Next on my list: catch an pikachu around Viridian Forest (rare) / Power Plant later. It grows into my raichu — that\'s my answer for Misty AND Lorelei down the line. Grabbing it now, before I need it.. THINGS YOU\'VE HEARD AND READ (from people and signs — your own notes, use them when they point somewhere): "Why don\'t you go upstairs and try trading POK.MON with your friends? You could get a lot more variety by trading. The POK.MON you get in trades grow quickly, to"; "Why don\'t you go upstairs and try trading POK.MON with your friends? You could get a lot more variety by trading. The POK.MON you get in trades grow quickly, to"; "That cruise ship S.S. ANNE is in VERMILION CITY. I hear there are lots of TRAINERS on board, too. They invited me to their party, but I can\'t stand fancy do\'s. "; "Wait till I get inside the TELEPORTER. When I do, go to my PC and run the Cell Separation System.". YOUR PLAN — right now: get abra and ekans to L16-17 then push to Cerulean City. Next: FIRST HM Surf — the prize of the Safari Zone\'s Secret House, deep in the back area. Surf opens the sea: Cinnabar, the Seafoam route, and Victory Road\'s water — the gym comes right after; that errand is the road. Bigger picture: Reach Cerulean City, beat Misty for the Cascade Badge. Your team right now: wartortle (L28), caterpie (L8), rattata (L12), spearow (L14), abra (L13), ekans (L12). Remember YOU are the one playing this — narrate your plan to chat in your own voice (first person: "I\'m grinding", "my team"), and never ask anyone what you\'re doing or who\'s on your team — you know.. RECALIBRATE — before the last detour you\'d set out to: "head toward the next gym - Misty of Cerulean City". That\'s still available. Unless something fundamental has actually changed, pick it back up and continue — don\'t lose the thread to aimless wandering.', 'progress': "1 badge(s) earned (Boulder). Next gym: Misty of Cerulean City. Pokédex: 7 caught. She's one badge in — the adventure's really starting (of 8 badges, then the Elite Four).", 'party': 'wartortle (L28), caterpie (L8), rattata (L12), spearow (L14), abra (L13), ekans (L12)', 'goal': {'short': 'get abra and ekans to L16-17 then push to Cerulean City', 'medium': "FIRST HM Surf — the prize of the Safari Zone's Secret House, deep in the back area. Surf opens the sea: Cinnabar, the Seafoam route, and Victory Road's water — the gym comes right after; that errand is the road", 'long': 'Reach Cerulean City, beat Misty for the Cascade Badge'}} options=['head_to_gym', 'talk_npc']

